The issue is that Django 2.2+ enforces unique db_table names across all models, but in your use case, you have multiple apps that use different databases and can legitimately have the same table names. The check should only enforce uniqueness for models that use the same database connection.

The fix should modify the `check_all_models` function in `django/core/checks/model_checks.py` to only check for duplicate db_table names among models that use the same database connection.

